text='''# Batch11 independent component review\n\nPASS for four new independent editable guest/service landing components, with the original ship still absent. Proposed catalogue count is61, including the preserved57 prior designs. This does not approve a room, lift, safe headroom, actor/cart route or target-engine behavior.\n\nActual source/native exchange checks passed for all four exports:4,548 new triangles, named editable geometry, correct source-to-native axes, finite UV/normal data, explicit material roles and byte-matched embedded textures. Individual staff control nodes and source/native physical marker normals were checked against actual geometry. All declared support/join witnesses, both full reused fixtures and their opposing mounts pass. The fixtures are QA context, not new designs.\n\nThe review caught and resolved exposed finish overlaps, bevel-edge bearing witnesses, a false cove-hull obstruction, a234mm false support-hull occupation, missing native datums, staff hatch/fixture interference, distance-dependent guest-art striping and unclear staff-control meaning. Failed/superseded evidence remains available. The exact-coplanar screen is explicitly limited: it did not catch the0.1mm layered art issue, which required actual640px pixels.\n\nAll seven declared empty boxes pass continuous triangle/box, source-solid containment and convex-compound feasibility checks with0.2mm boundary inset.533 finite clear/blocked paths also pass. Compounds remain approximate: observed guest seat/cushion corner inflation57.6mm is retained; staff small hardware/control relief is not fully covered. Profile sample maxima at<=35mm spacing are observations, not certified upper bounds or runtime acceptance.\n\nEight final component images and four r03 assembly images were inspected. Guest work reads as warm localized arrival/waiting furniture; staff work has practical washable fields, organized symbols/mounts and open retrieval space. The guest central approach remains visibly empty, and staff pieces retain a gap. The waiting-eye image is honestly oblique: the broad landmark is visible, but its fine text is not intended to be read from that angle. Intentional detail crops are separate from complete frames.\n\nCompleted fresh source-only executions regenerate all four GLBs byte-identically. Exact scripts, helpers, logs and all loaded shared/local image roles are bound. The guest art regeneration script also reproduces its PNG. No reviewer duplicate build was needed. Blender save-file byte equality is not claimed; source reload/semantic equivalence is recorded.\n\nThe61-row proposed interface index preserves every byte inside the old57 rows and binds183 current source/export/manifest files. The reviewer did not promote it. All1,279 protected previous asset/shared files and old57 raw catalogue rows remain unchanged. Lead owns final package validation, promotion and durable backup.\n\nPrimary receipts: independent_final_review.json, independent_final_source_hash_receipt.json, independent_interface_normalized_index_proposed.json, independent_rebuild_receipts.json, independent_assembly_visual_review.json.\n'''
